This file tells GitHub Pages to publish the repository verbatim instead of
running it through Jekyll.

Three things here need that:

  - 404.html has no YAML front matter, so Jekyll did not treat it as a page and
    it never reached the published site. A wrong URL fell through to GitHub's
    generic not-found page rather than the one written for this repository.

  - "Source Code" contains a space, and every path in the simulator's program
    index is built from it. Anything that rewrites or normalises those paths
    breaks all 525 links at once.

  - The simulator is plain ES modules loaded straight from disk. There is
    nothing to compile, so a build step can only get in the way.

The file is intentionally not empty: an empty file invites somebody to delete it
as leftover. Its contents are ignored.
